 "gaps": [
  "Missingness is not random and runs the wrong way. Twelve of the fourteen sunk, captured or set-afire vessels could not be sized, because the outcome that makes an incident severe is the same outcome that ends its AIS transmission. Severity by size therefore cannot be read off this dataset, and the apparent pattern that larger hulls absorbed hits better is unsupported.",
  "AIS static data is entered by the crew and describes the vessel now, not on the day it was attacked. A hull sold and re-registered since may broadcast different particulars.",
  "LOA is a shape, not a value. Deadweight, gross tonnage and hull value are what the insurance argument needs, and none of them are here.",
  "Three timeline rows (n=14 Norway, n=46 and n=50 Portugal) carry a country in the vessel field with flag Unknown - the same column-swap defect that houthi-timeline.json records as fixed for seventeen other rows. These three were missed and are excluded here.",
  "The ShipFinder search quota was exhausted on 2026-09-06, so the 25 named vessels with no MMSI on file could not be resolved. Retry the identity pass before treating coverage as final."
 ]
}
